  "question": {
    "text": "<div>Which of the following is the correct order of stability of conformations for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>OH</mi></math>.</div>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<div>gauche <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> eclipsed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> anti</div>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "gauche <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> anti <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> eclipsed",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "eclipsed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> gauche <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> anti",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "anti <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> eclipsed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#62;</mo></math> gauche",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The anti conformation is most stable in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OH</mi></math> groups are far apart as possible and minimum repulsion between two groups occurs.</p><p>In fully eclipsed conformation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>OH</mi></math> groups are so close that the steric strain is maximum.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0018_d5f62767d74f.png\" style=\"width: 513px; height: 219px;\" /></p><p>Since, gauche form is stabilised by intermolecular hydrogen bonding, hence it is more stable than anti.</p>"
  }
